WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.873 --> 00:00:10.856
For almost an hour, Amy Kim had been sitting in the audience at the middle school talent

2
00:00:10.857 --> 00:00:16.864
show, waiting for her turn to perform. She'd been watching the show. But mostly she'd been

3
00:00:16.865 --> 00:00:23.612
feeling nervous. Holding a deck of cards in her right hand, she practiced cutting the deck with

4
00:00:23.613 --> 00:00:37.024
one hand. Then she shifted the deck to her left hand and practiced that way. When that

5
00:00:37.025 --> 00:00:41.761
didn't calm her down, she shuffled the cards again and again. "Stop that!" her best friend, Megan

6
00:00:41.762 --> 00:00:47.417
Sanchez, hissed. "You're even making me nervous, and I don't get nervous before a show!" "Sorry!"

7
00:00:47.418 --> 00:00:54.916
Amy put the cards in her duffel bag and tried to concentrate on the talent show. But

8
00:00:54.917 --> 00:01:04.062
so many of the acts seemed the same. Except for one boy who played the clarinet, all

9
00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:15.145
the guys were in rock bands. The girls were either singing or dancing. Megan was scheduled

10
00:01:15.146 --> 00:01:19.070
to sing and dance later on, so she was wearing a long coat to conceal her costume.

11
00:01:19.071 --> 00:01:26.475
Amy had a top hat and wand in her bag. Megan glanced at the program and then

12
00:01:26.476 --> 00:01:34.721
nudged Amy. "Come on! It's time for us to get ready." "I can't believe I let

13
00:01:34.722 --> 00:01:42.380
you talk me into this," Amy said as they made their way backstage. Amy liked to do

14
00:01:42.381 --> 00:01:49.204
magic tricks, especially card tricks, and she sometimes performed for her family. But she'd been reluctant to

15
00:01:49.205 --> 00:01:58.102
perform in front of the whole school—until Megan persuaded her that it would be fun. "Remember what

16
00:01:58.103 --> 00:02:03.443
I told you. Don't think about the audience." Megan removed her coat to reveal a red

17
00:02:03.444 --> 00:02:14.034
leotard covered in sequins. "Think about the party afterward. So many of the boys in the show

18
00:02:14.035 --> 00:02:22.756
are coming!" "I'm glad I didn't eat any dinner because my stomach is churning. All I can

19
00:02:22.757 --> 00:02:31.575
hear is my heart pounding. Can you even hear me talking?" "You'll be fine once you

20
00:02:31.576 --> 00:02:40.990
get onstage." Megan gave Amy a quick hug before plopping down on the floor. "I sure hope

21
00:02:40.991 --> 00:02:48.656
so." Amy pulled her props from her duffel bag as she numbly watched Megan slipping into tap

22
00:02:48.657 --> 00:02:56.558
shoes. Amy had been practicing her act for days. She was planning to do three card

23
00:02:56.559 --> 00:03:09.549
tricks followed by two coin tricks. If the audience demanded an encore, she was sort of ready

24
00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:16.628
to pull some colored scarves from a paper cone. "I hope they don't want an encore,"Amy said

25
00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:21.870
to Megan. "I'm not too confident about that scarf trick." But Megan wasn't listening. Or rather, she

26
00:03:21.871 --> 00:03:25.885
wasn't paying attention to Amy anymore because she was listening to someone on her phone. Megan

27
00:03:25.886 --> 00:03:30.358
giggled. The plan was for Megan to act as Amy's assistant for the first card trick. Megan

28
00:03:30.359 --> 00:03:47.026
had suggested it. She said this would give Amy a chance to warm up and feel comfortable

29
00:03:47.027 --> 00:03:56.173
onstage. Then Amy would repeat the trick with a member of the audience. This would show

30
00:03:56.174 --> 00:04:05.016
that Megan hadn't helped her in any way. Amy watched from the wings as yet another group

31
00:04:05.017 --> 00:04:23.669
of guitar-playing boys worked their way through a popular song. The crowd was going wild. Amy glanced

32
00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:30.581
over at Megan, who was still on the phone. They were up next! "Megan!" Amy called. But

33
00:04:30.582 --> 00:04:43.794
her friend had a finger in one ear so she could hear better on the phone.

34
00:04:43.795 --> 00:04:51.978
The music stopped and the boys came offstage. Mr. Carlson, who was announcing the show and was

35
00:04:51.979 --> 00:05:00.288
also Amy's math teacher, started to introduce her act to the audience. Amy looked over at Megan,

36
00:05:00.289 --> 00:05:12.635
who was too busy laughing into the phone to notice her. "And now Amy Kim and

37
00:05:12.636 --> 00:05:26.538
her world of magic!" Mr. Carlson announced for the second time. Amy had no choice but to

38
00:05:26.539 --> 00:05:31.932
step onstage. The bright lights blinded her. "Uh," she said into the microphone. Then she glanced into

39
00:05:31.933 --> 00:05:40.101
the wings, hoping Megan would appear. "Uh," she said again. "This is an ordinary deck of

40
00:05:40.102 --> 00:05:47.259
cards. Nothing unusual about it at all. I'm now going to—" Megan suddenly rushed onstage, and someone

41
00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:53.338
whistled at her costume. "I'm here! Did I miss anything?" The audience laughed, but Amy flashed an

42
00:05:53.339 --> 00:05:59.835
annoyed look at her friend. But she tried to carry on as if nothing was wrong. "I'm

43
00:05:59.836 --> 00:06:06.184
now going to ask my assistant to pick a card, any card." Megan dutifully picked a

44
00:06:06.185 --> 00:06:10.973
card, just as they'd practiced so many times in Amy's bedroom. "Please look at it and show

45
00:06:10.974 --> 00:06:21.827
the audience," Amy said. Megan did as she was told, and Amy began to relax ever so

46
00:06:21.828 --> 00:06:30.819
slightly. "Now cut the cards as many times as you want, and I'll find your card."

47
00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:42.540
This was where things went suddenly, terribly wrong. As Megan cut the cards, she lost her grip

48
00:06:42.541 --> 00:06:50.374
on the deck. The cards scattered, with some even flying off the stage and into the audience.

49
00:06:50.375 --> 00:06:55.362
Amy's eyes widened in horror. There were some card tricks where the assistant is supposed to

50
00:06:55.363 --> 00:06:58.037
drop the cards into a pile instead of cutting the deck. But this wasn't one of them.

51
00:06:58.038 --> 00:07:05.179
Meanwhile the crowd was laughing wildly and getting louder by the minute. "Um, okay . . ."

52
00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:10.693
Amy stepped away from the microphone to pick up the cards. "We can't hear you!" someone in

53
00:07:10.694 --> 00:07:15.780
the audience shouted. Megan turned her back to the audience. "Just smile and keep going like

54
00:07:15.781 --> 00:07:21.351
nothing's wrong," she said to Amy. "They'll never know the difference." "Yes, they will!"Amy said in a

55
00:07:21.352 --> 00:07:29.191
surprisingly loud voice. "I can't believe you dropped the cards! All you had to do was cut

56
00:07:29.192 --> 00:07:37.088
them!" The kids in the front rows laughed. "What did you say?" someone called from the

57
00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:46.322
back of the auditorium. "We can't hear you!" "Louder!" someone else shouted. "Let's start again," Megan suggested.

58
00:07:46.323 --> 00:07:53.400
"No. Leave. I'll handle this myself," Amy said, though she had no idea how she was going

59
00:07:53.401 --> 00:07:58.992
to do that. Megan gave a big smile and waved to the crowd as she tap-danced

60
00:07:58.993 --> 00:08:07.557
offstage. Amy decided to abandon her card tricks and move on to the coin tricks. She pulled

61
00:08:07.558 --> 00:08:13.150
four quarters from her pocket. "As you can see, I have four ordinary quarters . . ."

62
00:08:13.151 --> 00:08:19.133
But she had forgotten to step back to the microphone, and no one could hear her. "Louder!

63
00:08:19.134 --> 00:08:26.038
Louder! Louder!" the crowd chanted. Amy looked out into the audience in terror. Then she turned

64
00:08:26.039 --> 00:08:34.841
and fled the stage. Megan was waiting in the wings. "You're still going to the party, right?"

